The pipeline discipline, workflow-orchestration mechanics (dependency-aware
escalating batches, per-batch circuit breaker, loop-until-dry extraction
with independent-referee verification), agent-boundary conventions
(read-only discovery agents vs. write-scoped execution agents), and
untrusted-input handling patterns (source code treated as data, credential
masking, injection-flag reporting) originate in code-modernization and are
reused here under the terms of the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The domain content — commands, agents, workflow scripts, and the
consistency-matrix viewer asset — has been substantially rewritten for a
different problem: harmonizing internal architecture/docs/pattern/style
divergence in an already-current, live codebase, as opposed to
code-modernization's legacy-to-modern migration of COBOL/legacy
Java/C++/.NET/monolith systems. No legacy-modernization domain content
(business-rule mining, COBOL/CICS/JCL parsing, dual-runtime equivalence
proving, version-delta cataloging) is carried over.

